  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Printer's Own Control Deck",
    "overview": "Each tool page is one machine. Its controls are built into the housing, and nothing is a loose card on the mat. The machine body is Leica satin silver in light and Leica black paint in dark, with a rolled edge all round, plates joined by seams, and names engraved into the plate and filled with paint. The bodies stand on a graph-paper mat in light and a cutting mat in dark. The nav unit rides a slim satin track at the left of the mat.\n\nThe parts are the parts kit: `app/kit.css` (every class has the `pk-` prefix), `components/hardware/kit/` (React parts) and `components/hardware/kit/slip.css` (paper). The parts get their depth from sprites rendered offline in one oblique light (`public/hardware/kit/`, `public/hardware/nav/`; each PNG carries its generator). Motion is short mechanical travel: a key goes down, a cap slides, a lever dips, a roller turns. Nothing fades or springs.\n\nThe user pinned these choices from the concept labs (units-refine, 2026-10-16). They are accepted and are the system:\n- one machine body per tool page, its controls in the housing;\n- satin silver and black paint bodies, engraved paint-filled lettering, rolled edges;\n- tape-deck keys in one well with a black legend strip, the red print key last;\n- counter windows with thumbwheels that step (buttons, scroll or arrow keys, never drag);\n- slide switches, short sliders and the red-dot shutter;\n- receipts at real size: a 320px slip with the print at 288px;\n- the nav unit on its track, with knurled rollers that turn as the page scrolls and stay still under reduced motion, and the current lever key dipped lengthwise;\n- Big Shoulders, Hanken Grotesk and Martian Mono.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "A printed mat (graph paper or cutting mat), never a flat fill.",
      "One body per page: a head plate with the engraved page name and the lamp, then plates and seams.",
      "Keys stand in one well under a black legend strip. The red print key is last.",
      "Counts and times read through counter windows on digit drums.",
      "Receipts at real size on white paper.",
      "Three accents with fixed jobs: red, green, orange."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Fixed Jobs Rule",
        "body": "Red marks only the current page (the flag window), printing, failures and errors, waiting jobs, the one print key, live audio in Tape and the Tape selection halo. Green is only the online LED. Orange is only the ON mark of a switch. The full list is in `docs/design-spec.md`, accent rules.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The On Is Not Red Rule",
        "body": "A slip that is on shows the switch position and its orange mark. A working slip is normal, not an alert.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Paper Stock Rule",
        "body": "Slip and thumbnail stock is `paper` in both themes. In dark, the room light dims it a little (`--pk-paper-light`). A preview of what will print (Studio, Photo) is exact: no grain, no dimming, no tilt on its pixels.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Capitals By CSS Rule",
        "body": "Write names, legends and stamps in sentence case in the source. CSS sets the capitals. Unit symbols keep their case (\"2 h\", \"274 px\").",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Engraving Floor Rule",
        "body": "Engraved and legend capitals are 10.5px or larger. Text that is read as a sentence is 14px or larger.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Engrave Or Type Rule",
        "body": "Names and legends are engraved on the plate. Values the user types or the machine reports show on a screen, a drum or paper.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Light Rule",
        "body": "All light comes from above, a little to the left. A gradient on a part models that light on its material and is never decoration.",
        "section": "elevation"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Soft Shadow Rule",
        "body": "Shadows are soft and close. Hard offset shadows are not part of this world.",
        "section": "elevation"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Sprite Rule",
        "body": "A part that has depth gets a sprite rendered in the kit's light, with its generator embedded. Do not draw a new part with CSS gradients.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do build a page as one body from the `pk-` parts and `components/hardware/kit/` before you write new CSS.",
      "Do put every theme value in a custom property on `:root` and override it under `html[data-theme=\"dark\"]`.",
      "Do engrave names and legends; show typed and reported values on a screen, a drum or paper.",
      "Do put the keys of a body in one well, with the red print key last.",
      "Do step a counter with its thumbwheel, scroll or arrow keys.",
      "Do show receipts at real size: a 320px slip, the print at 288px.",
      "Do give every control a 44px hit area.",
      "Do remove masks and blends under `forced-colors: active`, and stop transitions and the rollers under `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce`."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't put loose cards, bars or separate panels on the mat; a page is one machine.",
      "Don't use stat cards, pills, chips or a sidebar of icon links. A count reads through a counter window.",
      "Don't make a counter drag.",
      "Don't use hard offset shadows or gradients that do not model the kit's light.",
      "Don't make a key red unless it commits a print, and don't make On red.",
      "Don't use fades or springs; motion is short mechanical travel.",
      "Don't add a button that repeats the default action of an object that is already clickable.",
      "Don't set engraved capitals below 10.5px or reading text below 14px."
    ]
  }
}
